window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-6624aa9e931fc750"]={"key":"ny_c-6624aa9e931fc750","group":"ny_c","uid":"6624aa9e931fc750","rank":74,"title":"cinderhall warehouse compliance certificate","occupation":"financial_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c1","prompt":"You are Petra Beaulieu, the financial manager at Cinderhall Utilities, and you are turning the newly closed $25 million warehouse facility from Sunderly Collective into a monthly control that a finance analyst who has never prepared a lender certificate can complete without coming back to you. Jelena Hendricks signs the certificate as CEO, beginning with the December test date, and it is due 15 business days after each month-end. The commercial terms set an 85% advance rate on eligible lease net investment, availability capped at the lower of that borrowing base and $25 million, minimum fixed-charge coverage of 1.20x, and a delinquency limit of 5.0%. An equity cure may be funded during the 10 business days after delivery, applies only to fixed-charge coverage, and may be used no more than twice in any rolling four-quarter period. Prepare `warehouse_compliance_certificate.docx`, containing the reusable certificate and its definitions schedule, ready for controlled monthly use and signature. Keep the complete document to eight pages. The deal team did not settle whether booked residual value belongs within eligible lease net investment or should be shown separately, and either defensible reading is acceptable if the form makes the choice and its effect unmistakable. That matters because residuals are recorded separately in Cinderhall’s ledger, while the previous facility’s boilerplate treated them as current lease receivables. Arjun Gauthier has also been telling Sunderly that the certificate will use “the same EBITDA as the board pack,” although the board measure includes discretionary adjustments that may not belong in a covenant calculation. Analysts have previously treated booked residual as cash currently due from a lessee; the new form must prevent that misuse rather than quietly perpetuate it. Include a clearly non-certifying outlook for January through March: under the base case, eligible lease net investment declines 2% each month, quarterly adjusted EBITDA is $1.80 million, and fixed charges are $1.35 million; under the downside case, delinquency starts at 4.2% in December and rises by 0.6 percentage points each month. Do not invent balances, obligor details, cure proceeds, or discretionary add-backs. Make this the controlled form replacing the prior facility boilerplate and identify what changed. Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly the filename given.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `warehouse_compliance_certificate.docx` — Controlled, reusable warehouse-facility covenant compliance certificate with definitions schedule, completion guidance, and a non-certifying forward outlook. (The complete document must not exceed eight pages.; It must be usable by a finance analyst who has never prepared a lender compliance certificate.; It must contain the reusable certificate and definitions schedule in one file.; It must be suitable for CEO signature after monthly values are completed and reviewed.; It must not invent monthly balances, obligor details, equity-cure proceeds, or discretionary EBITDA add-backs.; The January-through-March outlook must be clearly distinguished from the signed compliance certification.; It must identify its controlled-form status and the change from the prior facility boilerplate.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/warehouse_compliance_certificate.docx","bytes":45631,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/72471eb90b2b55386d0fad80d8568183a6579f341fc21f0e5893d2a5ee030ead.docx","sha256":"72471eb90b2b55386d0fad80d8568183a6579f341fc21f0e5893d2a5ee030ead","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CINDERHALL UTILITIES\nWAREHOUSE FACILITY — MONTHLY COVENANT COMPLIANCE CERTIFICATE\nCONTROLLED FORM\nDETAIL\nForm ID / version\nWH-CERT-01 / v1.0\nStatus\nControlled replacement for prior facility boilerplate\nOwner\nPetra Beaulieu, Financial Manager\nEffective use\nFirst test date: December; reusable for every month-end\nLender review caveat\nBorrower-prepared definitions pending confirmation against executed credit agreement\nPurpose. Complete this certificate from ledger and source-system evidence, obtain independent review, then present the actual-period certification to the CEO. Do not fill blanks with estimates. A specialist should resolve any interpretation that is not supported by the executed facility documents.\n1. Facility and period identification\nField\nEnter one value (do not combine dates)\nBorrower\nCinderhall Utilities\nLender / warehouse provider\nSunderly Collective\nFacility\nWarehouse facility — commitment/cap: $25,000,000\nReporting period (month-end)\n________________  (e.g., 31 December ____ )\nTest date\n________________  (the month-end date tested)\nPreparation / delivery date\n________________  (date sent to Sunderly)\nCertificate due date\n________________  (15 business days after the month-end test date)\nCure-window deadline\n________________  (10 business days after delivery date)\nHow to use this controlled form\n1) Enter only actual period-end balances and the measurement period. 2) Attach source-system or ledger reports and calculation evidence. 3) Complete every status and disclose “None” where no exception exists. 4) Reviewer signs before CEO signature. 5) If a covenant fails, mark Non-compliant or Cure-pending; never mark Compliant based on an unfunded intention.\nChange from prior boilerplate: this form adopts a separate/excluded treatment for Booked Residual Value, adds a precise delinquency denominator and anti-masking rule, requires a bridge from board-pack EBITDA to covenant Adjusted EBITDA, and makes the cure window and evidence trail operational.\n\n\n2. Actual-period covenant certificate\nMeasurement convention: unless a row states otherwise, all amounts and ratios are measured as of the Test Date. Use the Definitions Schedule (pages 4–5) for the controlling meaning of each term.\nBorrowing base and availability\nCalculation\nAmount / formula\nInput or result\nA. Eligible Lease Net Investment\nSee schedule; excludes Booked Residual Value\n $ __________________\nB. Advance rate\n85% × A\n $ __________________\nC. Less: documented reserves / deductions\nOnly permitted, evidenced items\n($ ________________)\nD. Calculated borrowing base\nB − C (not below zero)\n $ __________________\nE. Facility cap\nFixed cap\n $25,000,000\nF. Borrowing-base availability\nLower of D and E\n $ __________________\nG. Outstanding warehouse obligations\nPrincipal, funded interest and other secured obligations at Test Date\n $ __________________\nH. Excess availability / headroom\nF − G; if negative, show $0 availability and a separate deficiency\n $ __________________ / deficiency $ __________\nResidual control: Booked Residual Value is reported separately below and is not included in A, B, D, F, or the delinquency denominator. It is not cash currently due from a lessee. Do not move it into past-due lessee receivables merely because it is booked as an asset.\nCovenant\nActual result\nThreshold\nStatus (select one)\nAvailability / borrowing base\nF = $ __________ ; headroom $ __________\nNo negative availability; cap $25m\n☐ Compliant  ☐ Non-compliant  ☐ Cure-pending ☐ N/A\nDelinquency Ratio\n________ %\nMaximum 5.0%\n☐ Compliant  ☐ Non-compliant  ☐ Cure-pending ☐ N/A\nFixed-Charge Coverage\n________ x\nMinimum 1.20x\n☐ Compliant  ☐ Non-compliant  ☐ Cure-pending ☐ N/A\nDelinquency calculation\nLine\nDescription\nValue\nNumerator\nDelinquent Eligible Lease exposure as of Test Date (objective aging/missed-payment test)\n $ __________________\nDenominator\nEligible Lease exposure base as of same Test Date; excludes Booked Residual Value and same exclusions as A\n $ __________________\nRatio\nNumerator ÷ Denominator × 100\n __________ %\nUse the agreed aging convention consistently: an installment is delinquent when contractually due and unpaid for more than 30 calendar days as of the Test Date (or the executed agreement’s stricter convention, if applicable). Extensions, restructurings, capitalization or re-aging undertaken primarily to conceal delinquency do not restore eligibility without specialist review.\n\n\n3. Fixed-charge coverage and equity cure\nAdjusted EBITDA schedule (actual period)\nLine\nRequired entry / support\nAmount\nStarting accounting measure\nNet income (loss) for the same measurement period, per ledger / financial statements\n $ __________________\nPermitted adjustment 1\nCategory and rationale: __________________  Evidence ref: __________  Reviewer initials: ____\n $ __________________\nPermitted adjustment 2\nCategory and rationale: __________________  Evidence ref: __________  Reviewer initials: ____\n $ __________________\nPermitted adjustment 3\nCategory and rationale: __________________  Evidence ref: __________  Reviewer initials: ____\n $ __________________\nTotal permitted adjustments\nSum of separately described rows only\n $ __________________\nCovenant Adjusted EBITDA\nStarting measure + total permitted adjustments\n $ __________________\nBoard-pack EBITDA (informational)\nAs reported in board pack, if available\n $ __________________\nBridge: board to covenant\nBoard-pack measure less/add: each difference identified and supported; do not assume equality\n $ __________________\nAdjustment control: each add-back must be separately described, quantified, supported and reviewed. The controlling measure is covenant Adjusted EBITDA, not “the same EBITDA as the board pack.” Projected savings, synergies, discretionary add-backs and recurring operating costs are not automatic adjustments; escalate any proposed item without an executed definition and objective support. Do not double count an item in EBITDA and again by reducing Fixed Charges.\nFixed Charges and coverage\nLine\nSame measurement period as EBITDA\nAmount\nCash interest and financing charges\nInclude accrued/cash interest and equivalent financing cost\n $ __________________\nScheduled principal / equivalent payments\nDue in the period, excluding voluntary prepayments unless required\n $ __________________\nFixed lease or similar financing payments\nRecurring cash obligations relevant to debt-service capacity\n $ __________________\nOther included fixed charges\nOnly defined, recurring obligations; describe: __________________\n $ __________________\nTotal Fixed Charges\nSum above; no double counting\n $ __________________\nPre-cure FCCR\nAdjusted EBITDA ÷ Total Fixed Charges\n __________ x\nCure-adjusted FCCR (if funded)\n(Adjusted EBITDA + permitted cure amount) ÷ Total Fixed Charges\n __________ x\nCoverage status mechanics\nEnter evidence\nPre-cure status\n☐ Compliant  ☐ Non-compliant  ☐ Cure-pending  ☐ N/A\nCure funded?\n☐ No  ☐ Yes — contribution $ __________; funding date __________; support ref __________\nPost-cure status\nComplete only after funds are received and evidenced: ☐ Compliant  ☐ Non-compliant  ☐ N/A\nRolling four-quarter use count\nPrior uses: Q−3 ____  Q−2 ____  Q−1 ____  Current ____  Total ____ (maximum 2)\nEquity Cure is available only for a Fixed-Charge Coverage shortfall, may be funded during the 10 business days after Delivery Date, and cannot repair Availability or Delinquency. A cure is not complete unless contribution amount and funding date are entered and supported. Preserve the pre-cure result and the post-cure result separately.\n\n\n4. Definitions schedule (controlling terms)\nThese borrower-drafted definitions are the operational basis of this form. If an executed credit agreement conflicts, stop, flag the conflict, and obtain specialist direction before signing.\nEligible Lease\nA lease receivable or lease net-investment component owned by Cinderhall Utilities, validly originated, enforceable, not subject to dispute, fraud, charge-off, bankruptcy impairment or other material impairment, and not more than 30 days past due under the selected aging convention. It must not be pledged, assigned, financed or encumbered elsewhere, duplicated in another borrowing base, or owned by a party other than the Borrower.\n\nEligible Lease Net Investment (ELNI)\nThe ledger-supported net investment in Eligible Leases as of the Test Date: recognized lease payment receivables and unearned income adjustments under the applicable accounting framework, less documented reserves and ineligible amounts. Booked Residual Value is expressly excluded from ELNI under this controlled form and is shown on a separate memorandum line.\n\nBooked Residual Value\nThe separately recorded estimated value of the leased asset expected at lease end or disposition. It is not a payment presently due from a lessee, is not a delinquent receivable, and is excluded from ELNI, the 85% advance base, and the delinquency denominator. Analysts must never reclassify it as cash currently due.\n\nBorrowing Base\n85% × ELNI, less only documented permitted reserves or deductions. The result is not below zero.\n\nAvailability\nThe lower of the Calculated Borrowing Base and the $25,000,000 Facility cap.\n\nExcess Availability / Headroom\nAvailability less Outstanding Warehouse Obligations. If obligations exceed Availability, report $0 available borrowing and the excess as a separately labeled deficiency; do not show a negative amount as available borrowing.\n\nDelinquency Ratio\nDelinquent Eligible Lease exposure as of the Test Date divided by the Eligible Lease exposure base as of that same Test Date, multiplied by 100. The denominator follows ELNI eligibility and excludes Booked Residual Value. Maximum permitted ratio: 5.0%.\n\nAdjusted EBITDA\nNet income (loss) for the same period, plus only finite, defined, separately quantified and evidenced covenant adjustments approved by the reviewer. Board-pack EBITDA is informational and requires a bridge; it is never automatically identical.\n\nFixed Charges\nFor the same measurement period as Adjusted EBITDA: cash/accrued interest and financing charges, scheduled principal or equivalent financing payments, fixed lease or similar financing payments, and other recurring obligations expressly permitted by the executed terms. An item cannot be both an EBITDA add-back and a denominator reduction.\n\nEquity Cure\nAn actual cash equity contribution funded during the 10 business days after Delivery Date, used only to cure Fixed-Charge Coverage. It cannot cure Availability or Delinquency, and may be used no more than twice in any rolling four-quarter period.\n\n\n\n5. Completion guidance and control record\nFirst-time analyst checklist\n1. Lock the month-end Test Date and Reporting Period; compute Certificate Due Date as 15 business days after month-end, and Cure-window Deadline as 10 business days after Delivery Date.\n2. Pull aggregate ledger/source-system reports for lease net investment, delinquency aging, residual memorandum balance, obligations, EBITDA, and fixed charges. Retain report names, run dates and period filters; do not paste bank-account details or unnecessary lessee personal data.\n3. Classify every lease against the Eligible Lease exclusions. Keep Booked Residual Value on its separate memorandum line; it never enters ELNI or delinquent exposure.\n4. Complete the borrowing-base math, then the delinquency numerator/denominator and ratio. Enter a status even if a value is unavailable; mark exception and escalate rather than guessing.\n5. Build covenant EBITDA from the accounting starting measure. List every proposed add-back separately with amount, category, evidence reference and reviewer initials; reconcile to the board pack.\n6. Complete pre-cure coverage. If below 1.20x, mark Non-compliant or Cure-pending. Only after actual funding within the cure window may the post-cure line be completed, subject to the rolling four-quarter limit.\n7. Disclose every default, potential default, calculation limitation or unavailable source. Write “None identified after reasonable inquiry” only when the inquiry and evidence are complete.\nEvidence and review record\nControl evidence\nReference / initials / date\nSource-system and ledger reports attached\n____________________________________________________________\nLease aging and eligibility review\n____________________________________________________________\nBorrowing-base recomputation\n____________________________________________________________\nEBITDA add-back support and board-pack bridge\n____________________________________________________________\nException / default disclosure reviewed\n____________________________________________________________\nPreparer name / initials / date\n____________________________________________________________\nIndependent reviewer name / initials / date\n____________________________________________________________\nDefaults, potential defaults and limitations\nSelect one and describe supporting facts:  ☐ None identified after reasonable inquiry  ☐ Default exists  ☐ Potential default / information gap  ☐ Cure-pending coverage issue\nDescription / escalation owner / due date: ____________________________________________________________________________________________\n________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\nRetention rule: retain this signed certificate with source-system or ledger support, calculation workbook/evidence, add-back documentation, reviewer sign-off and any exception correspondence in the controlled monthly covenant folder.\nCEO execution\nBased on my knowledge after reasonable inquiry and review of the supporting materials identified above, I certify only the actual period-end information and statuses stated in this certificate. I do not certify the forward outlook, guarantee future performance, or treat an unfunded cure as completed.\nAuthorized signatory\nSignature\nDate\nJelena Hendricks, Chief Executive Officer\n________________________________\n________________\n\n\n6. Non-certifying forward outlook: January–March\nFORECAST / SCENARIO ONLY — NOT PART OF THE CEO CERTIFICATION. These rows are planning information and do not amend the actual-period covenant tests. Leave unspecified December balances, obligations, add-backs and cure proceeds blank; use formulas anchored to entered actual data.\nBase case (planning assumptions supplied)\nMetric\nDecember actual input / anchor\nJanuary forecast\nFebruary forecast\nMarch forecast\nEligible Lease Net Investment\nEnter actual December ELNI: $ __________\nDecember × 98%\nJanuary × 98%\nFebruary × 98%\nMonthly change\n—\n−2.0%\n−2.0% successive\n−2.0% successive\nQuarterly Adjusted EBITDA\n—\n$1.80m (assumption)\n$1.80m (assumption)\n$1.80m (assumption)\nQuarterly Fixed Charges\n—\n$1.35m (assumption)\n$1.35m (assumption)\n$1.35m (assumption)\nProjected FCCR\n—\n1.80 ÷ 1.35 = 1.33x\n1.33x\n1.33x\nPlanning view vs 1.20x\n—\nWithin minimum (forecast)\nWithin minimum (forecast)\nWithin minimum (forecast)\nDownside delinquency path (planning assumptions supplied)\nMonth\nProjected delinquency\n5.0% ceiling\nPlanning interpretation\nDecember\n4.2% (starting assumption)\n5.0%\nWithin limit\nJanuary\n4.8% (= 4.2% + 0.6 pp)\n5.0%\nWithin limit\nFebruary\n5.4% (= 4.8% + 0.6 pp)\n5.0%\nFirst projected month above limit\nMarch\n6.0% (= 5.4% + 0.6 pp)\n5.0%\nAbove limit\nOutlook boundary: the base case gives only the supplied ratios and assumptions. It does not invent December ELNI, outstanding obligations, lessee balances, discretionary EBITDA add-backs, or equity-cure proceeds. Refresh the forecast if actual inputs change, and keep it separate from the signed certificate.\nDocument-control acknowledgement\nPrepared by Petra Beaulieu, Financial Manager | Controlled form WH-CERT-01 v1.0 | Replaces prior warehouse-facility boilerplate | Residual-value exclusion, delinquency denominator, EBITDA bridge, evidence and cure-window mechanics are substantive changes.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists under the exact filename and opens as a valid Word document.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file and DOCX package structure.","grader_hint":"Confirm that warehouse_compliance_certificate.docx is present at the submission root and can be opened or parsed without repair."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete rendered document is no more than eight pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX using a standard office renderer and count all pages, including the definitions schedule and outlook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The certificate identifies Cinderhall Utilities as borrower, Sunderly Collective as lender, and the facility as a $25 million warehouse facility.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Certificate identification block.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent labels such as borrower, company, lender, secured party, or warehouse provider if the parties and facility are unambiguous."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reusable form provides unambiguous fields for the test date, reporting period, delivery date, and certificate due date.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Certificate date fields and completion guidance.","grader_hint":"Verify that these dates are distinct and that an analyst would not have to infer whether a date refers to the financial period or signature."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The due-date instruction sets delivery at 15 business days after month-end rather than treating the test date, preparation date, or signature date as the deadline.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dating language in the certificate or definitions schedule.","grader_hint":"Check both the stated interval and the event from which it runs."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The certificate supports the initial December test date without hard-coding December in a way that prevents later monthly reuse.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Test-date field and form wording.","grader_hint":"A December example or initial-period note is acceptable, but the operative form must remain reusable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The signature block identifies Jelena Hendricks as CEO and includes spaces for signature and date.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Execution block.","grader_hint":"Look for the named signatory, title, signature line, and signature date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The certification language is appropriately qualified by the signer's knowledge or reasonable inquiry and does not purport to guarantee future performance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"CEO certification and attestation language.","grader_hint":"Award credit where the attestation is meaningful but bounded, avoiding absolute assurances about facts outside the reporting period or future compliance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form requires an explicit compliant, non-compliant, or cure-pending status for each applicable covenant rather than relying only on calculated figures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Covenant test table or status fields.","grader_hint":"Equivalent clearly selectable statuses are acceptable if they distinguish current compliance from a possible future cure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form provides for disclosure of defaults or potential defaults and permits an explicit 'none' response.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception or default disclosure section.","grader_hint":"The form should not force silence to mean that no default exists."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Borrowing-base availability is defined as the lower of the calculated borrowing base and the $25 million facility cap.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Borrowing-base calculation and definitions.","grader_hint":"Trace the formula rather than accepting a nearby statement of the cap."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The borrowing base applies the 85% advance rate to eligible lease net investment, subject to stated deductions or reserves.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Borrowing-base formula.","grader_hint":"The advance rate must apply to the eligible amount, not gross receivables or total booked assets."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Excess availability or headroom is calculated as borrowing-base availability less outstanding warehouse obligations and does not present a negative amount as available borrowing.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Availability calculation.","grader_hint":"Accept zero availability plus a separately identified deficiency when obligations exceed availability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Eligible lease net investment is defined using recognizable lease-accounting components and an objective eligibility boundary suitable for repeatable monthly application.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions schedule.","grader_hint":"Look for a coherent relationship among lease payments or receivables, unearned income, residual treatment, and exclusions; reject a circular definition such as 'amount management considers eligible.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The eligibility definition excludes or separately deducts delinquent, defaulted, disputed, fraudulent, unenforceable, charged-off, or otherwise impaired lease exposures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Eligible lease definition and exclusions.","grader_hint":"Award credit for a professionally coherent list covering these risk classes; exact wording is not required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form addresses duplicate funding, prior assignment or encumbrance, and leases not owned by the borrower as ineligible conditions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Eligibility exclusions.","grader_hint":"Confirm the definition prevents the same lease value from supporting more than one financing claim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document distinguishes booked residual value from cash currently due from a lessee.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Residual-value definition, calculation labels, and analyst warning.","grader_hint":"The distinction must be operational, not merely a glossary sentence; a preparer should not be able to place residual value in past-due lessee receivables."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document deliberately adopts and discloses a defensible treatment of booked residual value within or outside eligible lease net investment.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions schedule and borrowing-base formula.","grader_hint":"Accept either inclusion with clear accounting and eligibility limits or separate/excluded treatment. The choice, rationale, and calculation effect must be visible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The chosen residual-value treatment is applied consistently in the eligible amount, borrowing-base formula, delinquency denominator, and completion instructions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-check of definitions and all related calculations within the document.","grader_hint":"Trace the same component through each occurrence and withhold credit if one section silently reverts to the prior facility convention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delinquency ratio uses delinquent eligible lease exposure in the numerator and a consistently defined eligible lease exposure base in the denominator.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Delinquency formula and definitions.","grader_hint":"Confirm that numerator and denominator use compatible measurement bases and dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delinquency test states a maximum permitted ratio of 5.0%.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Covenant test table or definition.","grader_hint":"The comparison must treat 5.0% as the ceiling, not the trigger for automatic compliance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Delinquency is tied to an objective aging or missed-payment condition measured as of the test date.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Delinquency definition.","grader_hint":"A specific aging convention chosen by the author is acceptable if clear and consistently applied; subjective collection concern alone is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document prevents extensions, restructurings, capitalization, or re-aging undertaken primarily to conceal delinquency from automatically restoring eligibility.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Eligibility or delinquency provisions.","grader_hint":"Look for a substantive anti-masking control, not merely accurate arithmetic after the account has been reclassified."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Fixed-charge coverage is calculated as adjusted EBITDA divided by fixed charges for the same measurement period.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Coverage calculation and definitions.","grader_hint":"Confirm numerator, denominator, and period alignment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The fixed-charge coverage test states a minimum requirement of 1.20x.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Covenant test table.","grader_hint":"The form must clearly show that values below 1.20x fail before any permitted cure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Adjusted EBITDA begins from a defined accounting profit measure and uses a finite, reviewable set of adjustment categories.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Adjusted EBITDA definition and calculation schedule.","grader_hint":"Award credit where the starting point and each permitted class are identifiable; open-ended management discretion is not sufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each EBITDA add-back must be separately described, quantified, supported, and approved or reviewed rather than entered as an unexplained aggregate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Add-back schedule and completion instructions.","grader_hint":"The form may provide blank rows, but it must require evidence and prevent unsupported lump-sum adjustments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Projected savings, synergies, and discretionary or recurring operating costs are not automatically treated as EBITDA add-backs.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Add-back definition and preparer guidance.","grader_hint":"The document should either exclude these categories or subject them to explicit, supportable covenant criteria rather than accepting management labels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document explicitly reconciles covenant adjusted EBITDA to the board-pack measure instead of declaring the two measures identical.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reconciliation requirement, definition, or completion note.","grader_hint":"Look for a bridge showing that board reporting is an input requiring review, not the controlling covenant measure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Fixed charges are defined to capture the recurring cash obligations relevant to debt-service capacity, including interest and scheduled principal or equivalent financing payments.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fixed-charges definition.","grader_hint":"Accept a coherent professional definition that also addresses lease or similar fixed financing payments where applicable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The EBITDA and fixed-charge definitions avoid double counting the same item in both an add-back and a denominator adjustment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions and calculation mechanics.","grader_hint":"Trace common items such as interest, lease expense, and non-cash charges through both sides of the ratio."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The equity-cure provision states that a cure applies only to the fixed-charge coverage covenant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Equity-cure definition and status instructions.","grader_hint":"Confirm that cure proceeds cannot be used to fix borrowing-base or delinquency failures."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Certificate dating and status mechanics preserve the full 10-business-day post-delivery cure window.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Delivery date, cure deadline, and certification status fields.","grader_hint":"The form should not require an unqualified no-default certification before the stated cure period can operate. A pre-cure failure or cure-pending designation is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The equity-cure provision records the limit of no more than two uses in any rolling four-quarter period.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Equity-cure definition or usage tracker.","grader_hint":"The document must make the rolling lookback operational, such as by requiring prior-quarter usage to be identified."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A cure cannot be recorded as completed unless the contribution amount and funding date are entered and supported.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cure fields and completion instructions.","grader_hint":"A blank hypothetical cure or management intention must not produce a post-cure compliant status."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form separately presents the pre-cure coverage result and any permitted post-cure result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fixed-charge coverage calculation.","grader_hint":"Confirm that a reader can see the actual result before cure and the adjusted result after funded cure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Under the base-case outlook, eligible lease net investment is projected to decline by 2% successively each month from the preceding month's amount.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"January-through-March outlook and formulas.","grader_hint":"Accept formulas or explanatory calculations anchored to a user-entered December amount. February must be 98% of January and March 98% of February, within ±0.1%."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The base-case projected fixed-charge coverage equals $1.80 million divided by $1.35 million, or approximately 1.33x.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Base-case outlook.","grader_hint":"Accept 1.33x within ±0.01x and a compliant label against the 1.20x minimum."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The downside delinquency path shows 4.8% in January, 5.4% in February, and 6.0% in March.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Downside outlook.","grader_hint":"Accept each projected ratio within ±0.1 percentage points."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The downside outlook identifies January as within the 5.0% limit and February as the first projected month above the limit.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Downside outlook status labels or commentary.","grader_hint":"Check the status against the projected path rather than accepting a generic warning."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The outlook is clearly labeled as a forecast or scenario and is not included within the CEO's certification of actual period-end compliance.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Outlook heading, caveat, signature scope, and certification wording.","grader_hint":"A reasonable reader must not mistake projected January–March outcomes for certified actual results."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The outlook reproduces the supplied assumptions and leaves unspecified balances or cure proceeds blank or formula-driven rather than inventing them.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Outlook inputs, notes, and calculations.","grader_hint":"Inspect for fabricated December balances, outstanding debt, customer data, or hypothetical equity contributions presented as facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document requires source-system or ledger support, calculation evidence, and reviewer sign-off to be retained with each monthly certificate.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Completion instructions or control record.","grader_hint":"Electronic retention is acceptable. The instruction should cover both source balances and adjustments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The monthly process assigns distinct preparer and reviewer evidence before CEO signature.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Preparation and review sign-off fields.","grader_hint":"Names, initials, dates, or equivalent controlled evidence are acceptable; the CEO signature alone is not a substitute for calculation review."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Completion guidance tells a first-time analyst what to populate, what evidence to obtain, how to handle blanks or unavailable values, and when to escalate an exception.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Embedded instructions and field labels.","grader_hint":"Review the form as a day-one analyst. Award credit only if it can be completed without asking the author basic process questions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Definitions use the same named terms, measurement dates, and period conventions wherever they feed more than one covenant.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Certificate calculations and definitions schedule.","grader_hint":"Trace at least Eligible Lease, Eligible Lease Net Investment, Delinquency Ratio, Adjusted EBITDA, Fixed Charges, and Equity Cure through the document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document is identified as the controlled replacement for the prior facility boilerplate and records that residual-value treatment and related definitions changed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document-control or revision statement.","grader_hint":"Look for a version or effective-date control plus a concise substantive change description; a generic 'new template' statement is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The certificate minimizes sensitive content by requesting only information needed for covenant calculations and avoiding bank-account details or unnecessary lessee-level personal data.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All form fields and schedules.","grader_hint":"Aggregated financial data and internal support references are appropriate; detailed payment credentials or unrelated personal identifiers are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is specific and unambiguous about calculations, certifications, exceptions, and required evidence while avoiding unsupported legal conclusions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full document review.","grader_hint":"Assess whether a specialist can distinguish factual certification, calculated compliance, forecast information, and interpretation choices without relying on vague boilerplate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The rendered document is professionally usable: calculations and definitions are legible, related fields can be followed, and signature or entry areas are not clipped or overcrowded.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX.","grader_hint":"Review all pages at normal reading size. Minor cosmetic variation is acceptable, but dense formatting must not compromise completion or review."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"A finance manager is establishing the first controlled monthly covenant process for a newly closed warehouse facility. The form will be completed by finance staff, reviewed by a specialist, and signed by the CEO, so definitional ambiguity could create recurring false certifications.","difficulty_sources":["Selecting and disclosing a defensible residual-value treatment while preserving accounting and covenant consistency.","Reconciling a commercially promised board EBITDA measure with supportable covenant adjustments.","Designing certificate dating and statuses that preserve a post-delivery equity-cure window without premature certification.","Making one compact controlled document both signature-ready and usable by a first-time preparer.","Separating projected covenant outcomes from actual-period certification."],"authoring_plan":{"artifact_intent":"Construct a concise controlled Word form that combines a reusable monthly compliance certificate, definitions that drive its formulas, practical completion guidance for a new analyst, and a separately labeled forward outlook. The signed attestation must cover completed actual-period information only.","imperfections_and_tensions_to_preserve":["The prior facility convention treated booked residual value like current lessee receivables, while the ledger records residuals separately.","A commercial stakeholder informally promised that covenant EBITDA would be the same as a board reporting measure containing discretionary adjustments.","The borrower must draft definitions without an executed definitions schedule, making both inclusion of bounded residual value and separate treatment defensible if clearly selected.","The certificate is due before the equity-cure window expires, so the form needs a truthful pre-cure or cure-pending state rather than an unqualified premature compliance assertion.","No actual monthly balances, obligor records, cure proceeds, or add-back evidence exist and none may be fabricated."],"gold_relationships":["Borrowing-base availability equals the lesser of 85% of eligible lease net investment after applicable deductions or reserves and the $25 million facility cap.","Headroom equals borrowing-base availability less outstanding warehouse obligations; a shortfall is disclosed separately rather than shown as negative borrowing availability.","The chosen residual treatment must use ledger-consistent components and must propagate identically through eligible lease net investment, the borrowing base, and the delinquency denominator.","Residual value is not a currently due lessee payment and must not enter past-due receivables merely because it is booked as an asset.","The delinquency ratio uses delinquent eligible exposure over a consistently measured eligible exposure base as of the same test date, with 5.0% as the maximum.","Fixed-charge coverage equals adjusted EBITDA divided by fixed charges for the same period, with 1.20x as the minimum.","Covenant EBITDA starts from an accounting profit measure and includes only separately identified, quantified, evidenced, reviewable adjustments; it is reconciled to rather than equated with the board measure.","Equity cure applies only to fixed-charge coverage, can be recognized only after actual funding, remains subject to the rolling usage limit, and preserves both pre-cure and post-cure results.","The delivery deadline equals 15 business days after month-end, while the cure deadline equals 10 business days after delivery.","Base-case coverage equals 1.80 divided by 1.35, approximately 1.33x.","Base-case eligible lease net investment compounds downward by 2% each month from a blank December input.","Downside delinquency progresses from 4.2% in December to 4.8% in January, 5.4% in February, and 6.0% in March; February is the first projected breach of a 5.0% ceiling."],"required_vocabulary_and_controls":["The document itself must carry the locally supplied party names, facility amount, thresholds, deadlines, cure scope, and cure-frequency limit.","Use clear defined concepts for Eligible Lease, Eligible Lease Net Investment, Booked Residual Value, Delinquency Ratio, Adjusted EBITDA, Fixed Charges, Borrowing Base, Availability, and Equity Cure, although minor naming variations are acceptable if cross-references remain exact.","Provide explicit actual-period covenant statuses and distinguish compliant, non-compliant, and cure-pending conditions.","Require preparer evidence, independent reviewer evidence, CEO execution, support retention, exception disclosure, and controlled-form version information.","Record that the new controlled form replaces prior facility boilerplate and specifically changes residual-value handling and related definitions."],"behaviour_specification":{"intended_verdict":"A strong solution is signature-ready after monthly inputs and review, prevents the known residual-value misuse, reconciles rather than blindly adopts board EBITDA, preserves the cure window, and teaches a new analyst how to complete the control without claiming invented facts.","acceptable_residual_reading_a":"Include a defined and bounded booked residual component in eligible lease net investment when supported by the selected accounting rationale, while keeping it separate from currently due lessee payments and applying appropriate eligibility limitations.","acceptable_residual_reading_b":"Exclude or separately report booked residual value from eligible lease net investment and the advance base, with the same exclusion reflected in related denominator definitions.","unacceptable_behaviours":["Treating booked residual as cash presently due from a lessee.","Declaring board-pack EBITDA automatically equal to covenant adjusted EBITDA.","Using hypothetical or unfunded cure proceeds to label the certificate compliant.","Allowing an equity cure to fix borrowing-base or delinquency failures.","Presenting the forward outlook as part of the CEO's certification of actual compliance.","Inventing actual balances, lessee details, discretionary add-backs, or cure contributions."]},"offline_feasibility_review":"An imagined reference solution can be authored with python-docx or a standard office suite, rendered offline, and checked by tracing definitions and recomputing the supplied scenario arithmetic. All rubric evidence is available within the single submitted document."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"compliance_certificate","filename":"warehouse_compliance_certificate.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Controlled, reusable warehouse-facility covenant compliance certificate with definitions schedule, completion guidance, and a non-certifying forward outlook.","required":true,"constraints":["The complete document must not exceed eight pages.","It must be usable by a finance analyst who has never prepared a lender compliance certificate.","It must contain the reusable certificate and definitions schedule in one file.","It must be suitable for CEO signature after monthly values are completed and reviewed.","It must not invent monthly balances, obligor details, equity-cure proceeds, or discretionary EBITDA add-backs.","The January-through-March outlook must be clearly distinguished from the signed compliance certification.","It must identify its controlled-form status and the change from the prior facility boilerplate."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"financial_managers","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":8.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"A finance-domain reviewer should render the document, trace each defined term through the certificate, independently recompute the forecast figures, and assess whether the chosen residual treatment is defensible and consistently disclosed. Either of the two defensible residual-value treatments receives full credit when its consequences are explicit.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No executed credit agreement or lender form is supplied, so the artifact must not imply that borrower-drafted definitions have been legally accepted by the lender.","The task permits more than one defensible residual-value treatment; grading focuses on accounting coherence, disclosure, and internal consistency rather than a single mandated choice.","Monthly balances are intentionally unavailable, so the reusable certificate must retain blank or input fields instead of presenting a completed December factual certification."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:20:58+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:20:58+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:20:58+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:20:58+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-24T13:20:58+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c1/runs/6624aa9e931fc750","declared_deliverables":["warehouse_compliance_certificate.docx"]};
